  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FtF DRC Strengthening Value Chains</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Democratic Republic of the Congo):  The TBD Value Chains activity will aim to increase household incomes and access to nutrient-rich crops and cash crops by linking smallholder farmers to strengthened and inclusive value chains and supportive market services. The activity&apos;s focus is improved efficiency and inclusiveness of these value chains and expanded access to agricultural inputs, transportation, and financial services.. .FY 2021 funds will strengthen cooperative capacity, organize farmers into groups for training on improved post-harvest techniques and crop quality, facilitate access to finance, and improve market access. As one of several USAID activities co-located in South Kivu province, the TBD Value Chains activity will build upon and leverage complementary Bureau for Humanitarian Assistance Resilience Food Security Activities (RFSAs), health activities, and USAID&apos;s coordinated investments in governance. As a result, thousands of households will benefit from improved access to agricultural inputs and market systems...The TBD Value Chains activity will build the capacity and resilience of vulnerable populations to respond to shocks and stresses and take advantage of economic opportunities, contributing to the Mission&apos;s Integrated Country Strategy via Mission Goal 2 (Improved quality of life for Congolese through delivery of core services and expanded economic growth) and USAID&apos;s Country Development Cooperation Strategy via Development Objective 3 (Inclusive, broad-based, and sustainable economic growth increased). By supporting inclusive agricultural growth, improving the nutritional status of women and children, and increasing resilience in targeted communities, the activity will also support the Administration&apos;s Global Food Security Strategy and Feed the Future goals..</narrative>
  </description>
